Falsifies `memory_regions::proofs::a_reclaimed_subtree_leaves_no_count_behind`.

The defect: the claim gives back the claimed region's own slot and not the objects it still counts.
It reads as complete, because threads and spaces release themselves before the reclaim; the
rendezvous, notifications, timers and processes leave their tables only at the reclaim.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(after.live.get(counted) == 0, "a count outlived its
subtree")`, after any run that carved one of those kinds below the root.

